    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a challenging slate today, headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, who anchors the lineup with an elite 83.85 efficiency score. Benefiting from a favorable 4.01 xERA matchup against Trevor Rogers and a significant park factor boost, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is our clear \"must-start\" candidate. Also providing high-ceiling potential is **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), who exploits a soft matchup against Lucas Giolito (5.37 xERA). While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** draws a strong platoon advantage, **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) remains a primary pivot for stolen base production; his matchup against Melton and an aggressive batting order position allow him to capitalize on his high xwOBA despite the park-neutral environment.\n\nOur most difficult personnel decision involved the benching of **Brayan Rocchio** (47.66). While he narrowly missed the starting cut, the optimizer favored the higher raw projection and defensive floor of **Nasim Nunez** (62.09), whose switch-hitting ability remains vital despite his lower order spot. The Waves must navigate significant headwinds at the top of the order, specifically with **Gunnar Henderson** (53.01), **Kyle Tucker** (52.50), and **Andy Pages** (47.00) all drawing difficult assignments against elite arms in Macko (2.80 xERA) and Wheeler (2.86 xERA). While these stars are capable of producing against anyone, the proximity to the 40.0 \"Below Floor\" threshold for **Andy Pages** warrants close monitoring; any further dip in his game-day indicators may necessitate a shift toward **Coby Mayo** (47.14) in future rotations to optimize our daily efficiency caps.",
